# [DD-13b.W23.1] WHITESPACE-ONLY LINES AT FOUR POSITIONS — the INERT half
# of S0's rule, and the three positions the existing
# whitespace_only_line.rxtin (sem15) does not reach.
#
# Position 1 is between case lines (sem15's own). Positions 2, 3 and 4 —
# inside a `config` body, as the file's FIRST line, and immediately after a
# blank — are where the REJECTED "attachment-relevant" reading would have
# refused: under it S1's "attaches to nothing" arm fires on a
# whitespace-only first line and on one following a blank, both of which
# all three legs accept today.
#
# THE ASSERTION IS THAT THE PARSE IS IDENTICAL to the same file with these
# lines deleted, not merely that the file is accepted.
   
config dev
  flags i
   
  engine vm

   
description a file with whitespace-only lines in four places

pattern a+
m "aaa" 0 3
   
n "b"
